AI kit — vibecode with JRebirth
===============================

JRebirth ships an **AI kit**: a small set of files that tell coding agents how the framework expects you to structure an application. It works with Cursor, Claude Code, Codex, Copilot, and similar tools.

You do not need to be an AI specialist. You do not need to memorize every JRebirth API either. Install the kit in your project, then ask the agent for a screen, a command, or a service in plain language.

## What problem it solves

Agents are good at producing JavaFX code. Left alone, they often invent patterns that fight JRebirth: `Platform.runLater` everywhere, business logic in controllers, or `getCommand(...).run(...)`.

The kit gives them a fixed contract:

- which role owns which code (Model, View, Controller, Command, Service, Wave, …)
- how threading works (JavaFX thread vs background work)
- how to message between components (Waves)
- step-by-step skills for common tasks

## What you install

The kit lives in the JRebirth repository under `jrebirth-ai-kit/`:

| File / folder | Role |
|---------------|------|
| `AGENTS.md` | Short, strict rules for any agent |
| `CLAUDE.md` | Points Claude Code at `AGENTS.md` |
| `.cursor/rules/jrebirth-core.mdc` | Cursor rule for `*.java` / `*.fxml` |
| `skills/jrebirth-*/` | Task skills (`SKILL.md` + code samples in `references/`) |
| `install.ps1` / `install.sh` | Copies or links the kit into your app |
| `install-interactive.ps1` / `install-interactive.sh` | Same installer with prompts (target path, link, force) |

One source of truth — no second maintained copy of the same skills elsewhere.

