## Download the kit (ZIP)

You can install without cloning the full JRebirth repository:

1. Download **[${aiKitZip}](downloads/${aiKitZip})** from this site (rebuilt with each `${project.version}` site publish).
2. Unzip anywhere on your machine.
3. Run the interactive installer (recommended) or call `install` directly.

**Windows (interactive)**

```text
Expand-Archive ${aiKitZip} -DestinationPath C:\tools
cd C:\tools\jrebirth-ai-kit
.\install-interactive.ps1
```

**Linux / macOS (interactive)**

```text
unzip ${aiKitZip} -d ~/tools
cd ~/tools/jrebirth-ai-kit
chmod +x install-interactive.sh install.sh
./install-interactive.sh
```

The prompts ask for your **application project path** (where `AGENTS.md` and skills should land), whether to **symlink** skills, and whether to **force-replace** existing agent files.

#[[

## Install in your project (Git clone)

From a clone of [JRebirth](https://github.com/JRebirth/JRebirth):

**Windows**

```text
cd jrebirth-ai-kit
.\install.ps1 -Target C:\path\to\your-app
```

**Linux / macOS**

```text
cd jrebirth-ai-kit
chmod +x install.sh
./install.sh /path/to/your-app
```

The installer puts `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` at the root of your app (it asks before overwriting), installs the Cursor rule, and publishes skills under `.cursor/skills`, `.claude/skills`, `.codex/skills`, and `.agents/skills`.

Use `--force` / `-Force` to replace existing agent files (a `.bak` is kept). Use `--link` / `-Link` to junction/symlink the skills folder instead of copying.

Details and the full skill list: see `jrebirth-ai-kit/README.md` in the repository.

## How to work with an agent

1. Install the kit once in the app repo.
2. Ask for a concrete feature in everyday language.
3. Let the agent open the matching `jrebirth-*` skill before it writes code.
4. Review the result like any other PR: roles, threading, and naming should match `AGENTS.md`.

### Example prompts

- “Scaffold a membership list screen with JRebirth MVC.”
- “Add a SaveMembershipCommand and wire the Save button through the controller.”
- “Load members from our REST API in a Service, then refresh the table with a wave.”
- “This class mixes UI and HTTP calls — refactor it into JRebirth roles.”

## Skills at a glance

| You want to… | Skill |
|--------------|--------|
| Decide where code belongs | `jrebirth-core` |
| Create a full screen | `jrebirth-create-mvc` |
| Add Model / View / Controller | `jrebirth-create-model`, `…-view`, `…-controller` |
| Add a Command or Service | `jrebirth-create-command`, `jrebirth-create-service` |
| Call a Command safely | `jrebirth-invoke-command` |
| Fix thread / `runLater` issues | `jrebirth-threading` |
| Bootstrap a Maven app | `jrebirth-maven-project` |
| Fix `module-info` / ModuleStarter | `jrebirth-jpms-module` |

The README in the kit lists every skill with a sample prompt.

## What this is not

- Not a replacement for the [framework documentation](Toc.html).
- Not a magic “generate my whole product” button — you still own design and review.
- Not tied to one vendor: the same `AGENTS.md` and skills are meant for several agent tools.

